ed_at":"2025-12-12T09:18:18Z","pushed_at":"2025-12-10T21:49:12Z","git_url":"git://github.com/forem/forem.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:forem/forem.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/forem/forem.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/forem/forem","homepage":"https://forem.com","size":1725259,"stargazers_count":22543,"watchers_count":22543,"language":"Ruby","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":true,"has_wiki":true,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":true,"forks_count":4153,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":555,"license":{"key":"agpl-3.0","name":"GNU Affero General Public License v3.0","spdx_id":"AGPL-3.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/agpl-3.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTE="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["community","discussion","feedback","hacktoberfest","open-source","rails","ruby"],"visibility":"public","forks":4153,"open_issues":555,"watchers":22543,"default_branch":"main","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/forem/forem/pulls/22615","html_url":"https://github.com/forem/forem/pull/22615","diff_url":"https://github.com/forem/forem/pull/22615.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/forem/forem/pull/22615.patch","merged_at":"2025-11-20T19:49:06Z"},"body":"\r\n  # Add validation to check if comment has readable content after markdown processing\r\n\r\n  - Reject comments that only contain markdown formatting symbols (e.g., ** **, _ _, ~~ ~~)\r\n  - Add error message: 'cannot be empty. Please enter some text before submitting.'\r\n  - Add comprehensive test coverage for various markdown-only scenarios\r\n\r\n  Fixes #22572\r\n\r\n  ## What type of PR is this? (check all applicable)\r\n\r\n  - [ ] Refactor\r\n  - [ ] Feature\r\n  - [x] Bug Fix\r\n  - [ ] Optimization\r\n  - [ ] Documentation Update\r\n\r\n  ## Description\r\n\r\n  This PR prevents users from creating empty comments by adding a validation that checks for actual text\r\n  content after markdown processing.\r\n\r\n  ### Problem\r\n  Users could submit comments containing only markdown formatting symbols (like `****` for bold or `---`\r\n  for horizontal rules) without any actual text, resulting in empty or meaningless comments being created.\r\n\r\n  ### Solution\r\n  Added a `body_has_content` validation to the `Comment` model that:\r\n  1. Strips HTML tags from the processed HTML output\r\n  2. Checks if there's any actual text content remaining\r\n  3. Rejects the comment with a user-friendly error message if only formatting is present\r\n\r\n  ### Changes Made\r\n  - **Model**: Added `body_has_content` validation method in `app/models/comment.rb`\r\n  - **I18n**: Used existing translation at `config/locales/models/en.yml:49`\r\n  - **Tests**: Added comprehensive test coverage in `spec/models/comment_spec.rb`\r\n\r\n  ## Related Tickets & Documents\r\n\r\n  - Closes #22572\r\n\r\n  ## QA Instructions, Screenshots, Recordings\r\n\r\n  ### Testing Steps:\r\n  1. Navigate to any article on the site\r\n  2. Click to add a comment\r\n  3. Try to submit a comment using only formatting:\r\n     - Type `****` (bold formatting)\r\n     - Or type `** **` (bold with space)\r\n     - Or type `---` (horizontal rule)\r\n  4. **Expected**: You should see an error message: \"Body markdown cannot be empty. Please enter some text\r\n   before submitting.\"\r\n  5. Now type actual text with formatting: `**Hello world**`\r\n  6. **Expected**: Comment should be successfully created\r\n\r\n  ### Test Cases Covered:\r\n  - ❌ Rejects: `****` (only bold markers)\r\n  - ❌ Rejects: `** **` (bold markers with space)\r\n  - ❌ Rejects: `---` (horizontal rule)\r\n  - ✅ Accepts: `**Hello world**` (text with bold formatting)\r\n  - ✅ Accepts: `_Hello world_` (text with italic formatting)\r\n  - ✅ Accepts: `**Bold** and _italic_ text` (mixed formatting)\r\n  - ✅ Accepts: `Hello world` (plain text)\r\n\r\n  ### UI accessibility checklist\r\n  _Not applicable - no UI changes, validation message only._\r\n\r\n  ## Added/updated tests?\r\n\r\n  - [x] Yes\r\n  - [ ] No, and this is why: _please replace this line with details on why tests have not been included_\r\n  - [ ] I need help with writing tests\r\n\r\n  ### Test Coverage:\r\n  Added 7 new tests in `spec/models/comment_spec.rb`:\r\n  - 3 tests for invalid cases (formatting-only comments)\r\n  - 4 tests for valid cases (comments with actual text)\r\n  - All tests passing ✅\r\n\r\n  ## [optional] Are there any post deployment tasks we need to perform?\r\n\r\n  No post-deployment tasks required. The validation runs automatically on comment creation.\r\n\r\n  ## [optional] What gif best describes this PR or how it makes you feel?\r\n\r\n  ![Blocking empty content](https://media.giphy.com/media/3o7btNhMBytxAM6YBa/giphy.gif)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/forem/forem/issues/22615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/forem/forem/issues/22615/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":21080062402,"node_id":"CE_lADOBGPKJs7XjUvvzwAAAAToeDnC","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/forem/forem/issues/events/21080062402","actor":{"login":"benhalpern","id":3102842,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDI4NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3102842?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/benhalpern","html_url":"https://github.com/benhalpern","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benhalpern/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benhalpern/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benhalpern/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benhalpern/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/benhalpern/su